gonna be held at Roboworld.

175
00:17:50,487 --> 00:17:52,614
I can't believe they're allowing this.

176
00:17:52,614 --> 00:17:54,533
That's just it. They're not.

177
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:55,576
Thought so.

178
00:17:55,576 --> 00:18:00,706
That's why KURUKURU=DAZA
and SHOTO=O-JIN dropped out.

179
00:18:00,706 --> 00:18:03,709
I was gonna be in it for fun, you know?

180
00:18:03,709 --> 00:18:08,463
There's no way I'm gonna race
while I get attacked by some army!

181
00:18:08,463 --> 00:18:10,465
Good point.

182
00:18:10,465 --> 00:18:14,636
I'm a racer now, not a soldier:
I've had enough of that shit.

183
00:18:15,721 --> 00:18:17,723
I can't do it.

184
00:18:17,723 --> 00:18:20,976
Roboworld is an important client
of my kingdom.

185
00:18:20,976 --> 00:18:23,478
I'm not ready to give up
my life just yet.

186
00:18:24,855 --> 00:18:29,484
So after the popularity poll,
the top 2 teams were picked.

187
00:18:33,989 --> 00:18:35,490
I see...

188
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:40,871
JP, are you going?

189
00:18:40,871 --> 00:18:42,789
Or will you drop out?

190
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:44,541
JP, please make a statement!

191
00:18:44,541 --> 00:18:46,668
I take it back, Frisbee.

192
00:18:47,044 --> 00:18:49,004
Fix up the Trans-Am, will you?

193
00:18:49,004 --> 00:18:49,588
What?

194
00:18:49,588 --> 00:18:51,840
So you're going, then?

195
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:54,551
Is that official, JP?
He won't.

196
00:18:54,551 --> 00:18:57,054
Please give us a comment, JP! A simple yes or no!
Think twice before you say something.

197
00:18:57,054 --> 00:18:58,555
Please give us a comment, JP! A simple yes or no!

198
00:18:58,555 --> 00:19:00,474
Give me the camera.

199
00:19:02,225 --> 00:19:04,936
Watch out, Roboworld! Here comes JP!

200
00:19:06,605 --> 00:19:11,360
All right! He's in! JP's in! And there you
have it from JP who has qualified for REDLINE.

201
00:19:11,568 --> 00:19:15,322
Oh goody! It's time for the festival of fools again!

202
00:19:15,322 --> 00:19:17,366
I like rough sports every now and then.

203
00:19:25,791 --> 00:19:27,876
PAROLE

204
00:19:28,293 --> 00:19:28,502
SATELLITE EUROPASS

205
00:19:28,502 --> 00:19:33,006
SATELLITE EUROPASS
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

206
00:19:33,006 --> 00:19:33,590
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

207
00:19:34,299 --> 00:19:38,178
Please prepare for landing in your designated pod.

208
00:19:40,138 --> 00:19:44,142
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

209
00:19:44,351 --> 00:19:46,770
Please prepare for landing in your designated pod.

210
00:19:57,406 --> 00:20:00,200
Wow! It's picking up speed.

211
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:03,286
Flaps... Flaps...
Where's the flaps button?

212
00:20:08,917 --> 00:20:11,002
Is this a coffin or what?!

213
00:20:11,002 --> 00:20:16,425
This is nothing but a serious act
of aggression against Roboworld!

214
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:19,094
Secretary Titan!

215
00:20:19,094 --> 00:20:19,553
Si"

216
00:20:19,553 --> 00:20:22,222
You must have something to report!

217
00:20:22,222 --> 00:20:24,850
I just received a message from our scout vessels.

218
00:20:24,850 --> 00:20:30,147
They identified a group of ships on Europass's surface.

219
00:20:30,439 --> 00:20:31,940
Europass?

220
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:32,649
Yes.

221
00:20:32,649 --> 00:20:36,611
The planet we donated to those pathetic refugees.

222
00:20:36,611 --> 00:20:43,869
It's demilitarized under our treaty
with the M3 Nebula Federation.

223
00:20:43,869 --> 00:20:45,912
That means our forces must tread very carefully there.

224
00:20:46,163 --> 00:20:50,584
Besides, the refugees from
nearby sectors have drifted in...

225
00:20:50,584 --> 00:20:53,170
and set up slums all over the place.

226
00:20:53,378 --> 00:20:57,299
It's an ideal hideout for REDLINE racers.

227
00:20:58,008 --> 00:21:00,719
This is what we get
for being so generous!

228
00:21:03,013 --> 00:21:07,267
They have the audacity to claim it's
by the viewers' request.

229
00:21:07,267 --> 00:21:12,522
Don't they know we can't put
our military secrets at risk?

230
00:21:12,522 --> 00:21:16,443
There's no way we'd allow
a stupid race in such a sacred place!

231
00:21:16,443 --> 00:21:18,737
Mr. President.

232
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,243
Are you all right, sir?

233
00:21:26,953 --> 00:21:28,622
Mr. President!

234
00:21:28,622 --> 00:21:29,414
What?

235
00:21:29,414 --> 00:21:32,626
You're not going to stand by and let them pass, are you?

236
00:21:32,626 --> 00:21:34,836
I make the rules on this planet!

237
00:21:34,836 --> 00:21:39,549
All those affiliated with REDLINE are
guilty and deserve to be hanged!

238
00:21:39,549 --> 00:21:41,676
As president, I'll take full responsibility!

239
00:21:41,676 --> 00:21:44,805
Because I represent justice.

240
00:21:44,805 --> 00:21:47,933
The entire universe is in need of strong leadership,

241
00:21:47,933 --> 00:21:54,272
and Roboworld stands
heroically by its principals!

242
00:21:55,357 --> 00:21:57,859
Colonel Volton!

243
00:21:57,859 --> 00:21:58,777
Si"

244
00:21:58,777 --> 00:22:01,446
Are you ready to shed your blood for justice?

245
00:22:01,446 --> 00:22:03,240
Sir! More than ready, sir!

246
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:07,661
Good! Fight with your life for ultimate justice!

247
00:22:08,703 --> 00:22:10,330
Thank you, sir!

248
00:22:17,838 --> 00:22:18,672
Hey, you!

249
00:22:19,923 --> 00:22:20,966
Hey, I'm talking to you!

250
00:22:20,966 --> 00:22:24,302
Don't you ignore me!
Buy a ticket for REDLINE, will ya?

251
00:22:25,011 --> 00:22:26,096
Don't ignore me!

252
00:22:26,096 --> 00:22:28,473
You have money, don't you?

253
00:22:30,267 --> 00:22:33,061
How about I give you a discount?

254
00:22:33,770 --> 00:22:35,939
What happened there?

255
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:38,733
Get off me.

256
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:40,193
What happened?

257
00:22:40,193 --> 00:22:43,405
Stop it! Sorry to disappoint,
but I'm not here to watch.

258
00:22:44,573 --> 00:22:46,408
Useless! You're so totally useless to us!

259
00:22:46,408 --> 00:22:47,951
Ahh...fuck!

260
00:22:48,743 --> 00:22:49,619
Wait!

261
00:22:50,579 --> 00:22:54,457
1, 2, s, 4...

262
00:22:58,545 --> 00:22:59,379
Next!

263
00:23:00,881 --> 00:23:02,257
What is this?

264
00:23:02,257 --> 00:23:04,676
You're sure about the exchange rate?

265
00:23:04,676 --> 00:23:06,177
Just about right. Next!

266
00:23:06,970 --> 00:23:09,598
Just about? What the heck is that?

267
00:23:09,598 --> 00:23:11,433
You need to take money more serious...

268
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:12,475
You're annoying!

269
00:23:22,611 --> 00:23:23,528
Right here.

270
00:23:24,863 --> 00:23:25,906
What?

271
00:23:25,906 --> 00:23:27,282
Need some smokes.

272
00:23:27,282 --> 00:23:27,866
Got money?

273
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:32,078
Sure. I just cashed in.

274
00:23:32,078 --> 00:23:35,165
Give me as many as this will get.

275
00:23:40,712 --> 00:23:41,588
Here.

276
00:23:42,756 --> 00:23:44,633
What, is this it?

277
00:23:44,633 --> 00:23:46,009
It's already open.

278
00:23:47,302 --> 00:23:49,512
This ain't right.

279
00:23:49,512 --> 00:23:51,848
Hey, Grandma!
Money needs to be taken...

280
00:23:52,098 --> 00:23:54,726
Don't like it? Then leave it.

281
00:23:54,726 --> 00:23:57,562
Just leave it and walk away!

282
00:24:04,194 --> 00:24:04,778
Huh?

283
00:24:12,452 --> 00:24:13,536
Whoops.

284
00:24:17,666 --> 00:24:19,209
Whoa! Whoa!

285
00:24:21,962 --> 00:24:24,297
View's clear!

286
00:24:25,131 --> 00:24:28,259
Good. Let's roll!

287
00:24:34,641 --> 00:24:35,600
Nice!

288
00:24:35,892 --> 00:24:37,769
These antigravity engines aren't bad!

289
00:24:38,561 --> 00:24:41,147
Yeah, not bad at all!

290
00:25:01,793 --> 00:25:02,627
Done.

291
00:25:07,257 --> 00:25:09,217
Oh, it's you, JP.

292
00:25:09,217 --> 00:25:11,386
This planet is really something, huh?

293
00:25:11,386 --> 00:25:12,762
What did you expect?

294
00:25:12,762 --> 00:25:16,349
This place gets flotsam from all over the galaxy.

295
00:25:16,349 --> 00:25:20,020
It's hard for the idea of service to sink in.

296
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:21,604
How are you holding up?

297
00:25:23,898 --> 00:25:25,442
Alright, I guess... Ouch!

298
00:25:26,109 --> 00:25:27,902
Yeah, I can see that.

299
00:25:32,365 --> 00:25:33,491
Ow... Ow...

300
00:25:36,244 --> 00:25:40,331
I got an attaché case from Frisbee.
It was stuffed with cash.

301
00:25:40,331 --> 00:25:42,250
Yeah, it's for fixing up
the Trans-Am.

302
00:25:42,250 --> 00:25:46,755
He used to drop everything
to work on your machine.

303
00:25:47,005 --> 00:25:49,507
He sure has changed.

304
00:25:49,507 --> 00:25:51,843
Like you, me, and everything else.

305
00:25:51,843 --> 00:25:55,513
Cigs cost more and good junk joints
are harder to find.

306
00:26:02,187 --> 00:26:04,272
So, where's my Trans-Am?

307
00:26:15,283 --> 00:26:18,453
You really did it this time,
you ingrate.

308
00:26:18,453 --> 00:26:21,956
What were you thinking,
using the nitro twice?

309
00:26:21,956 --> 00:26:24,626
You got a death wish?

310
00:26:25,335 --> 00:26:27,504
I'll need three caps for the REDLINE.

311
00:26:28,546 --> 00:26:29,464
Three?!

312
00:26:29,798 --> 00:26:31,716
Hey, watch it, Pops!

313
00:26:32,133 --> 00:26:34,594
This is a totally different level
than the YELLOWLINE.

314
00:26:34,594 --> 00:26:37,680
I'm gonna need an edge, won't I?

315
00:26:37,847 --> 00:26:40,350
Then get your machine armed up.

316
00:26:40,350 --> 00:26:44,604
You know that
anything goes at REDLINE.

317
00:26:44,604 --> 00:26:46,606
I can get you armed up good.

318
00:26:46,606 --> 00:26:49,484
REDLINE's a race, not a war.

319
00:26:49,484 --> 00:26:51,236
Keep that crap off of my machine.

320
00:26:51,236 --> 00:26:54,948
I see you're as stupidly soft
as your nickname implies.

321
00:26:54,948 --> 00:26:56,699
Don't call me that!

322
00:26:56,699 --> 00:27:00,912
In the REDLINE, you can attack or
interfere with the others any way you want.

323
00:27:00,912 --> 00:27:05,458
You're behind the times
by trying to play fair.

324
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:07,627
Behind the times, huh?

325
00:27:08,837 --> 00:27:15,093
30 years in this business and
I still got my chops. Not bad, huh?

326
00:27:15,093 --> 00:27:19,806
I clean up good with all
the trades I get at the race.

327
00:27:19,806 --> 00:27:23,893
A little fun on the side wouldn't hurt, either.

328
00:27:23,893 --> 00:27:26,187
A little fun.

329
00:27:27,147 --> 00:27:28,523
Listen, JP.

330
00:27:29,607 --> 00:27:32,819
If you want a stove that'll stand up to 3 caps of juice,

331
00:27:32,819 --> 00:27:35,029
you're talking a redesign from scratch.

332
00:27:35,029 --> 00:27:36,906
If you don't want to use weapons,

333
00:27:36,906 --> 00:27:40,660
all I can do is to get you
a new engine and custom parts.

334
00:27:40,660 --> 00:27:43,329
I wish I could do more.

335
00:27:43,329 --> 00:27:45,665
Hey, you listening to me?

336
00:27:46,291 --> 00:27:48,251
Frisbee can handle
the redesigning and tune-up.

337
00:27:48,501 --> 00:27:49,711
You're joking.

338
00:27:49,711 --> 00:27:50,628
Huh? Why?

339
00:27:52,589 --> 00:27:55,049
When was the last time
you two worked as a team?

340
00:27:55,049 --> 00:27:55,758
Stop it.

341
00:27:55,758 --> 00:27:57,760
Frisbee's not legit anymore.

342
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,762
Cut it out!
He's sold out. He's no good!

343
00:27:59,762 --> 00:28:00,680
He's sold out. He's no good!

344
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:08,521
Talking about the fix?

345
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:13,067
He's not the same man. You know that, right?

346
00:28:13,067 --> 00:28:16,321
Helping an ingrate like you is no big deal,

347
00:28:16,321 --> 00:28:19,449
but getting mixed up with that scum is another story.

348
00:28:19,449 --> 00:28:22,035
Racers and mechanics
gotta stick together.

349
00:28:22,744 --> 00:28:26,289
You and I make a good team.
Always have.

350
00:28:27,123 --> 00:28:28,791
Hey, Frisbee.
Took you long enough.

351
00:28:29,209 --> 00:28:33,630
I may be a scum,
but I still got the touch, you know.

352
00:28:33,630 --> 00:28:35,798
Don't judge a man's skill by his character.

353
00:28:36,716 --> 00:28:40,553
So, you've also learned to
sneak around now, Frisbee?

354
00:28:43,014 --> 00:28:44,432
Relax, Pops.

355
00:28:44,432 --> 00:28:47,727
If I didn't have the touch,
I wouldn't still be here.

356
00:28:48,561 --> 00:28:51,231
Nobody's worried about your touch.

357
00:28:53,650 --> 00:28:55,026
The old man's on board.

358
00:28:55,026 --> 00:28:57,153
I didn't agree to anything.

359
00:28:57,153 --> 00:28:59,405
Hey, quit that!

360
00:28:59,405 --> 00:29:01,324
I guess I'll leave it to the two of you now.

361
00:29:01,324 --> 00:29:02,867
Hey! Where are you going?

362
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:08,122
The old man will get a new engine.

363
00:29:08,122 --> 00:29:11,292
Frisbee'll take care of the redesign and mods.

364
00:29:11,292 --> 00:29:14,671
I'll do my job when I put my butt behind the wheel.

365
00:29:15,505 --> 00:29:17,674
Until then, I'll leave everything to you pros.

366
00:29:18,508 --> 00:29:20,301
Like the old days.

367
00:29:21,844 --> 00:29:23,846
He think he's cool or something?

368
00:29:40,905 --> 00:29:42,031
What do you want?

369
00:29:43,825 --> 00:29:46,035
This ain't your seat, punk!

370
00:29:46,035 --> 00:29:47,537
You want some?!

371
00:29:48,788 --> 00:29:52,875
Oh, a comb...
Don't scare me, you fool!

372
00:29:52,875 --> 00:29:56,045
I see you're having a full house today, waiter.

373
00:29:56,045 --> 00:29:57,672
I'm the manager, you jerk!

374
00:29:57,672 --> 00:29:59,841
And enough with the wisecracks!
The place is deserted.

375
00:29:59,841 --> 00:30:02,885
Just pick a table and settle down, will ya?

376
00:30:02,885 --> 00:30:03,678
Okay, okay.

377
00:30:04,387 --> 00:30:06,472
Sorry about that, Miss.

378
00:30:07,557 --> 00:30:11,477
He won't bother you anymore,
so don't worry.

379
00:30:12,228 --> 00:30:15,606
Here's your soup spaghetti
a la Europass lobster.

380
00:30:15,606 --> 00:30:17,025
Looks great!

381
00:30:17,025 --> 00:30:18,693
Enjoy your meal.

382
00:30:18,693 --> 00:30:19,902
Thank you.

383
00:30:28,661 --> 00:30:31,080
You're breaking the dress code, Manager.

384
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:33,082
Oh, no! How embarrassing!

385
00:30:33,082 --> 00:30:34,250
What are you doing?

386
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:35,209
Nothing.

387
00:30:35,209 --> 00:30:36,794
No, seriously.

388
00:30:37,754 --> 00:30:40,298
Excuse me. I'm JP.

389
00:30:40,298 --> 00:30:41,591
JP?

390
00:30:41,591 --> 00:30:42,967
Are you gonna eat that?

391
00:30:42,967 --> 00:30:43,676
Huh?

392
00:30:44,969 --> 00:30:45,553
What's this?

393
00:30:50,975 --> 00:30:51,934
Give me a break...

394
00:30:52,602 --> 00:30:54,937
Mind if I join you?

395
00:30:55,271 --> 00:30:57,440
Sorry, I'm waiting for someone.

396
00:30:58,358 --> 00:30:59,067
Bummer.

397
00:31:00,109 --> 00:31:05,198
I remember now!
You're that guy from the YELLOWLINE.

398
00:31:05,198 --> 00:31:07,867
You're going to REDLINE
as a substitute, right?

399
00:31:07,867 --> 00:31:08,451
What do you want?

400
00:31:10,161 --> 00:31:14,207
I thought I'd check you out
since you're going, too.

401
00:31:14,207 --> 00:31:14,916
Come again?

402
00:31:17,168 --> 00:31:18,378
She saw my underpants...

403
00:31:18,378 --> 00:31:21,839
Winning the YELLOWLINE with a hover engine...

404
00:31:21,839 --> 00:31:25,093
was so cool that I wanted to
check out the racer for myself.

405
00:31:25,093 --> 00:31:26,386
And the verdict?

406
00:31:27,470 --> 00:31:30,139
Verdict? Well...

407
00:31:30,139 --> 00:31:34,519
I see an engine geek with no interest in men.

408
00:31:34,519 --> 00:31:35,436
Bingo.

409
00:31:35,436 --> 00:31:39,941
Wheels are my only love.
I've known nothing but racing since I was a kid.

410
00:31:40,149 --> 00:31:43,945
So, you're one of those sad types who
can't make any human friends, huh?

411
00:31:44,779 --> 00:31:47,031
Meaning what?
Why don't you just go now?

412
00:31:52,870 --> 00:31:54,664
My dad was a racer.

413
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:57,250
We owned a junk joint.

414
00:31:57,250 --> 00:31:59,961
We used to build our own
machines to enter races.

415
00:32:00,711 --> 00:32:01,587
I see.

416
00:32:03,423 --> 00:32:07,218
It was the most natural thing to do...

417
00:32:07,218 --> 00:32:08,136
What's that?

418
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:12,723
Steamlight. Isn't it pretty?

419
00:32:13,558 --> 00:32:16,727
My Dad gave it to me on my 7th birthday.

420
00:32:18,896 --> 00:32:22,358
So this is a steamlight, huh?
I've never seen one before.

421
00:32:22,358 --> 00:32:25,153
They say when burned as fuel,

422
00:32:25,153 --> 00:32:28,573
it releases 100 times more energy
than gold nitro.

423
00:32:28,573 --> 00:32:29,991
No kidding.

424
00:32:30,199 --> 00:32:33,244
This is my first time seeing real steamlight, too.

425
00:32:33,953 --> 00:32:36,164
An energy source with unlimited capacity.

426
00:32:37,165 --> 00:32:42,003
No man can handle that
amount of power, though.

427
00:32:42,003 --> 00:32:43,546
You know a lot, don't you?

428
00:32:43,546 --> 00:32:46,799
Oh, how do you do.
I'm Shinkai.

429
00:32:46,799 --> 00:32:48,384
Pleased to meet you.

430
00:32:48,384 --> 00:32:51,846
Aren't you gonna eat that?
Hexagonal worm spaghetti soup.

431
00:32:51,846 --> 00:32:52,972
It's so good!

432
00:32:53,806 --> 00:32:55,266
Please have some.

433
00:32:55,266 --> 00:32:56,058
Hooray!

434
00:32:57,351 --> 00:32:59,979
May I perhaps taste some of you as well tonight?

435
00:33:03,357 --> 00:33:04,484
Yummy time!

436
00:33:05,443 --> 00:33:08,529
She would have been mine
if you hadn't interrupted.

437
00:33:08,529 --> 00:33:10,364
Mr. Substitute.

438
00:33:11,199 --> 00:33:12,783
Call me a reserve.

439
00:33:13,910 --> 00:33:17,705
You guys are racers, right?
I saw you on the news.

440
00:33:17,705 --> 00:33:19,749
I'm a racer myself, you know.

441
00:33:19,749 --> 00:33:23,377
Though I must say I'm more known as a mechanic.

442
00:33:23,377 --> 00:33:27,006
I have a partner named Trava.

443
00:33:27,006 --> 00:33:28,007
Trava?

444
00:33:29,967 --> 00:33:31,177
Let me go!

445
00:33:33,679 --> 00:33:36,349
Stop trashing the place! Take it outside!

446
00:33:37,141 --> 00:33:38,476
Trava!

447
00:33:38,476 --> 00:33:39,519
Your partner?

448
00:33:39,519 --> 00:33:41,604
The one getting beaten up, yes.

449
00:33:41,604 --> 00:33:42,730
Which one is that?

450
00:33:44,482 --> 00:33:46,817
Hey, that hurt!

451
00:33:46,817 --> 00:33:48,528
You started it.

452
00:33:48,861 --> 00:33:51,030
Shit! Here he goes!

453
00:33:51,280 --> 00:33:53,449
It's your fault, damn it!

454
00:33:53,449 --> 00:33:55,660
You betrayed the army.

455
00:33:55,660 --> 00:33:58,162
Is the tough guy crying?

456
00:33:58,162 --> 00:33:59,997
That's Little Deyzuna.

457
00:33:59,997 --> 00:34:03,543
He used to be in the army with us.

458
00:34:03,543 --> 00:34:06,087
He becomes impossibly strong when he cries.

459
00:34:15,555 --> 00:34:18,057
Having a race on Roboworld!

460
00:34:18,057 --> 00:34:20,977
You're just doing that to make me suffer!

461
00:34:22,478 --> 00:34:23,938
That's bullshit!

462
00:34:23,938 --> 00:34:26,065
It's nothing personal and you know it!

463
00:34:26,065 --> 00:34:27,608
Liar!

464
00:34:43,291 --> 00:34:45,710
Hm. More weirdoes on the scene.

465
00:34:50,172 --> 00:34:54,093
Well, if it ain't Machine Head Tetsuzin himself.

466
00:34:54,093 --> 00:34:55,886
That's really Machine Head?

467
00:34:57,388 --> 00:34:59,724
Mr. REDLINE.
The fastest man in the galaxy.

468
00:35:04,395 --> 00:35:05,479
Outta my way.

469
00:35:06,397 --> 00:35:07,982
Don't order me around!

470
00:35:08,232 --> 00:35:10,568
I said, outta my way!

471
00:35:10,568 --> 00:35:13,487
You think you can order me around?

472
00:35:13,779 --> 00:35:15,781
I'm just telling you to move.

473
00:35:15,781 --> 00:35:17,700
That's an order, you moron!

474
00:35:17,700 --> 00:35:21,245
Fine, if you won't move,
I'll go around you.

475
00:35:25,416 --> 00:35:29,086
That's what you get
when you mess with me!

476
00:35:29,086 --> 00:35:31,005
To hell with the race!

477
00:35:48,439 --> 00:35:49,607
Sonoshee!

478
00:35:52,151 --> 00:35:53,277
This way!

479
00:36:17,968 --> 00:36:18,928
What?

480
00:36:18,928 --> 00:36:20,471
Looks like Roboworld forces.

481
00:36:33,567 --> 00:36:36,487
You're a hard man to find,
Little Deyzuna.

482
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:40,032
Colonel Volton!

483
00:36:40,032 --> 00:36:43,119
You weren't ordered
to leave the base.

484
00:36:43,536 --> 00:36:46,706
I told you to stay put, didn't I?

485
00:36:46,706 --> 00:36:48,666
Look what you did!

486
00:36:55,172 --> 00:36:57,174
Thanks for coming here personally...

487
00:36:57,174 --> 00:37:00,469
to deal with your insubordinate
subordinate, Col. Volton.

488
00:37:01,220 --> 00:37:02,263
Stay there!

489
00:37:03,889 --> 00:37:08,561
This is a demilitarized zone.
We won't stand for this.

490
00:37:08,561 --> 00:37:10,438
So what?

491
00:37:10,438 --> 00:37:12,106
I said so what?

492
00:37:12,106 --> 00:37:16,235
Are Roboworld soldiers
hard of hearing?

493
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:24,160
Oh, I can hear you fine.
I just don't need your permission.

494
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:26,704
Doesn't matter. I got what I came for.

495
00:37:26,704 --> 00:37:31,208
Oh, yes, and I have orders to
use force on the day of the race.

496
00:37:31,208 --> 00:37:32,376
Seriously?!

497
00:37:32,376 --> 00:37:34,879
Volton's Hell Troops have been
ordered into action?

498
00:37:43,304 --> 00:37:49,185
The president generously offered
his presence at your silly race.

499
00:37:49,185 --> 00:37:54,148
You should try to be good targets
for our troops in return.

500
00:37:54,148 --> 00:37:57,276
I suppose having your heads can wait.

501
00:37:57,276 --> 00:37:57,902
Hey, you!

502
00:37:58,694 --> 00:38:01,530
Don't try something stupid.

503
00:38:07,578 --> 00:38:11,832
The air in here's kinda stuffy
since you guys walked in.

504
00:38:12,708 --> 00:38:13,709
Beat it.

505
00:38:15,419 --> 00:38:19,215
You've got seven guns
pointed at you.

506
00:38:20,549 --> 00:38:22,176
Nice. That'll solve my...

507
00:38:27,681 --> 00:38:28,474
Ow.

508
00:38:42,071 --> 00:38:43,155
Ow!

509
00:38:43,155 --> 00:38:44,907
That hurts...

510
00:38:44,907 --> 00:38:46,116
How's your head?

511
00:38:46,992 --> 00:38:48,536
I'll live.

512
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:51,080
What were you thinking?

513
00:38:51,080 --> 00:38:55,751
Those bastards were really trying my patience.

514
00:38:56,126 --> 00:38:57,294
Couldn't help it.

515
00:38:58,087 --> 00:39:01,257
