Please take a look.

770
00:54:56,377 --> 00:54:58,254
Hey, Lynchman.

771
00:54:58,254 --> 00:54:59,047
What?

772
00:54:59,047 --> 00:55:02,550
Why did the REDLINE Commission
put us up to this?

773
00:55:02,842 --> 00:55:05,845
If the hyper-disintegrator
blasts everyone to hell,

774
00:55:05,845 --> 00:55:09,057
there won't be any race.
That means no betting.

775
00:55:09,057 --> 00:55:10,558
I see.

776
00:55:10,558 --> 00:55:11,434
Get in.

777
00:55:13,603 --> 00:55:16,397
That won't be good for the fat cats.

778
00:55:16,397 --> 00:55:18,775
You know how much money is riding on this?

779
00:55:18,775 --> 00:55:20,235
No idea.

780
00:55:20,235 --> 00:55:22,570
Enough to buy out a couple of planets.

781
00:55:22,570 --> 00:55:23,571
Oh, wow!

782
00:55:23,571 --> 00:55:27,617
Besides, it's gonna be
great publicity for them.

783
00:55:27,617 --> 00:55:32,539
REDLINE's odds'll go up,
and so will their margins.

784
00:55:32,539 --> 00:55:33,748
I get it.

785
00:55:35,500 --> 00:55:37,669
So this is our target for today?

786
00:55:37,669 --> 00:55:39,671
You got it!

787
00:55:46,344 --> 00:55:50,431
The main power station's system was attacked...

788
00:55:50,723 --> 00:55:54,102
...by pro-REDLINE guerrillas
consisting of low-level workers.

789
00:55:59,524 --> 00:56:01,317
As a result, the RED-RACERS...

790
00:56:01,317 --> 00:56:04,946
are now safe from
heavy ground-based weaponry.

791
00:56:04,946 --> 00:56:08,533
Roboworld officials are currently
working on corrective measures.

792
00:56:08,533 --> 00:56:12,537
According to government sources,
the malfunction of the power system...

793
00:56:12,537 --> 00:56:15,665
...occurred late last night.
When the Robopolice arrived...

794
00:56:46,279 --> 00:56:46,946
What's your name?

795
00:56:49,198 --> 00:56:50,700
JP?

796
00:56:50,700 --> 00:56:51,576
Where did you get that?

797
00:56:51,576 --> 00:56:52,911
Weird name.

798
00:56:52,911 --> 00:56:53,786
I'm Sonoshee.

799
00:56:53,786 --> 00:56:54,621
Sonoshee.

800
00:57:17,393 --> 00:57:20,021
With REDLINE just a day away,

801
00:57:20,021 --> 00:57:25,485
we should keep our eyes on the
racers trying to enter Roboworld.

802
00:57:25,485 --> 00:57:29,781
For this non-stop road race
in the military exercise base,

803
00:57:29,781 --> 00:57:32,492
each driver's course pick will hold the key.

804
00:57:33,368 --> 00:57:37,664
We've been profiling the
REDLINE racers every evening.

805
00:57:37,664 --> 00:57:40,625
On the eve of the big race,
we feature JP,

806
00:57:40,625 --> 00:57:44,629
who's entering only because
another racer dropped out.

807
00:57:44,629 --> 00:57:48,383
Like Lynchman, who's notorious
for his rough play,

808
00:57:48,383 --> 00:57:50,635
JP has a dark past of his own.

809
00:57:50,635 --> 00:57:52,553
According to our research,

810
00:57:52,553 --> 00:57:58,059
this man with a nickname of “Sweet JP“

811
00:57:58,059 --> 00:58:03,439
was indeed a race-fixing
specialist in the past.

812
00:58:03,731 --> 00:58:05,525
What the hell?

813
00:58:06,150 --> 00:58:09,988
This is REDLINE, a festival awaited by
young and old every 5 years.

814
00:58:09,988 --> 00:58:13,908
We need to make sure all concerned
parties are aware of the fact that...

815
00:58:15,994 --> 00:58:18,579
Lucky for me.
It's still running.

816
00:58:22,250 --> 00:58:24,502
REDLINE FINALS DAY

817
00:58:32,385 --> 00:58:34,262
What was that?

818
00:58:34,262 --> 00:58:37,098
I think it's the Supergrass' scout vessel.

819
00:58:37,098 --> 00:58:40,977
The army of that wicked wizard princess, eh?

820
00:58:40,977 --> 00:58:44,063
So, they've teamed up with
the REDLINE now, have they?

821
00:58:44,522 --> 00:58:47,400
Easy does it, easy...

822
00:58:47,567 --> 00:58:49,360
Easy, easy...

823
00:58:49,360 --> 00:58:50,403
Slop!

824
00:58:50,778 --> 00:58:55,074
Too bad you have to race without a test run.

825
00:58:55,074 --> 00:58:56,784
I'll be fine.

826
00:58:57,493 --> 00:58:58,327
JP!

827
00:58:58,327 --> 00:58:59,412
Yeah?

828
00:58:59,412 --> 00:59:00,872
You know the drill, right?

829
00:59:01,039 --> 00:59:03,624
What I know is that it's my show now.

830
00:59:18,431 --> 00:59:20,224
What's that red smoke?

831
00:59:39,994 --> 00:59:40,995
Ta-d ah!

832
00:59:41,621 --> 00:59:43,289
Nice work, Princess.

833
00:59:43,498 --> 00:59:44,082
Piece of cake.

834
00:59:44,082 --> 00:59:45,208
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
Piece of cake.

835
00:59:45,208 --> 00:59:47,752
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
Now, all we have to do is to wait for the start.

836
00:59:47,752 --> 00:59:50,129
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
We're going there to win, alright?

837
00:59:50,880 --> 00:59:56,761
I've just received word
that Supergrass' Red Angels...

838
00:59:56,761 --> 00:59:59,806
have successfully marked the
finish line by the Roboworld Tower.

839
01:00:01,224 --> 01:00:03,142
That's our princess!

840
01:00:03,142 --> 01:00:04,727
I guess she made it.

841
01:00:04,727 --> 01:00:06,145
Of course.

842
01:00:06,145 --> 01:00:09,398
She's the only one who can use remote magic.

843
01:00:09,857 --> 01:00:12,235
We must make her proud.

844
01:00:15,363 --> 01:00:16,531
Morning, Sonoshee!

845
01:00:17,406 --> 01:00:19,742
Looks like you're mad at me.

846
01:00:19,742 --> 01:00:22,912
Not really...
We're rivals now anyway.

847
01:00:22,912 --> 01:00:25,915
Once we're on the race track,
friendship won't count.

848
01:00:25,915 --> 01:00:27,208
I guess you're right.

849
01:00:27,208 --> 01:00:28,126
Uh huh.

850
01:00:32,547 --> 01:00:33,339
Sonoshee.

851
01:00:33,339 --> 01:00:35,925
Three minutes to drop zone.

852
01:00:37,343 --> 01:00:38,511
Good luck, then.

853
01:00:40,847 --> 01:00:42,849
You see the transport ship?

854
01:00:42,849 --> 01:00:43,599
Yes, Mr. President.

855
01:00:44,308 --> 01:00:48,104
Let's say the line marked by
our HQ is the finish line.

856
01:00:48,104 --> 01:00:53,276
At 800 km west above the expected
start line at Knockout Tower,

857
01:00:53,276 --> 01:00:57,196
we detected an energy reading
from a hyperdimensional drive.

858
01:00:57,196 --> 01:00:58,990
Hyperdimensional drive?

859
01:01:00,116 --> 01:01:03,578
How dare they violate our airspace
using a navigation method...

860
01:01:03,578 --> 01:01:07,123
that's only supposed
to exist in theory!

861
01:01:07,123 --> 01:01:10,376
I'll teach those RED-RACERS a lesson!

862
01:01:11,294 --> 01:01:15,131
Titan! Arm the disintegrator cannons!

863
01:01:15,131 --> 01:01:16,007
Yes, sir!

864
01:01:34,066 --> 01:01:35,776
Bought your ticket yet?

865
01:01:35,776 --> 01:01:37,778
Hey! You put it all on Sonoshee.

866
01:01:37,778 --> 01:01:39,739
Yeah! Sonoshee's my girl.

867
01:01:39,739 --> 01:01:41,073
You're the man!

868
01:01:41,073 --> 01:01:42,033
Give me those pork buns!

869
01:01:42,033 --> 01:01:43,201
Only three left.

870
01:01:43,201 --> 01:01:44,410
Fine.

871
01:01:44,410 --> 01:01:45,995
Hey, you! You betting or not?

872
01:01:45,995 --> 01:01:48,956
Not yet. I'm waiting for the final odds.

873
01:01:48,956 --> 01:01:49,916
Hot!

874
01:01:49,916 --> 01:01:53,711
Ew! What a mess!
You're supposed to eat them in one bite.

875
01:01:53,711 --> 01:01:56,255
Okay guys, last call!

876
01:01:56,255 --> 01:01:58,049
Anyone who wants to buy in,
step up now.

877
01:01:58,049 --> 01:02:00,676
One minute to the start!
I'm closing now!

878
01:02:00,676 --> 01:02:01,802
Give me JP!

879
01:02:02,011 --> 01:02:04,055
One minute to drop point.

880
01:02:04,055 --> 01:02:06,599
All racers, please prepare for the drop.

881
01:02:21,155 --> 01:02:23,407
Deploying apogee motors
on hyper-disintegrator cannons.

882
01:02:44,679 --> 01:02:48,516
95% energy level.
Stand by on firing button.

883
01:02:49,892 --> 01:02:52,436
Please put on your light shield, sir.

884
01:02:53,813 --> 01:02:56,774
Entering drop zone.

885
01:03:00,319 --> 01:03:03,322
We have an energy reading
on the transport ship.

886
01:03:03,322 --> 01:03:05,366
It's out of hyperdimensional drive.

887
01:03:05,366 --> 01:03:07,493
Put it on the monitor.

888
01:03:09,161 --> 01:03:11,580
Open fire upon visual contact.

889
01:03:12,164 --> 01:03:13,332
Aye, aye, sir.

890
01:03:25,845 --> 01:03:27,763
Hyper-disintegrator cannons, fire!

891
01:03:27,763 --> 01:03:28,681
Firing!

892
01:03:38,232 --> 01:03:40,651
What's wrong?
Why aren't they firing?

893
01:03:43,195 --> 01:03:44,405
We have a malfunction.

894
01:03:44,405 --> 01:03:46,240
What?! That's unacceptable!

895
01:04:24,528 --> 01:04:27,156
Good morning, all you lucky fans
gathered here today.

896
01:04:27,156 --> 01:04:29,241
After five years of waiting,
it's the day of the big race!

897
01:04:29,241 --> 01:04:32,620
We're broadcasting live to the cosmos
for all you crazy fans out there!

898
01:04:33,204 --> 01:04:35,581
The Red-Machines are being
airdropped to start the race...

899
01:04:35,581 --> 01:04:38,542
and heading straight toward Knockout Tower.

900
01:04:38,542 --> 01:04:40,378
If you're looking for a long shot,
here's your man!

901
01:04:40,378 --> 01:04:42,755
JP with his trademark ducktail.

902
01:04:42,755 --> 01:04:45,841
His odds are a whopping
25,000 to 1!

903
01:04:45,841 --> 01:04:48,469
What's going on with that hair?

904
01:04:48,469 --> 01:04:50,388
But his machine's just as impressive.

905
01:04:50,388 --> 01:04:51,931
You see every kind of design
imaginable in this race,

906
01:04:51,931 --> 01:04:55,184
but I don't think anyone's
ever modified a car like JP.

907
01:04:55,184 --> 01:04:58,938
Looks great. Sweet dedication
from the sweet man.

908
01:04:58,938 --> 01:05:02,066
Dedication? Maybe.
Or maybe his hair is affecting his brain.

909
01:05:03,317 --> 01:05:06,779
Calling the race is me,
the rattle-king Void Do.

910
01:05:06,779 --> 01:05:10,658
And here for commentary is
former RL champ, Mr. Minerva Hanness.

911
01:05:10,658 --> 01:05:12,159
Stay tuned!

912
01:05:12,159 --> 01:05:14,078
Damn that REDLINE...

913
01:05:14,078 --> 01:05:17,623
Mr. President, let my Voltan Corps
take over from here.

914
01:05:17,623 --> 01:05:19,750
All right.
Show them what you've got!

915
01:05:20,584 --> 01:05:22,628
Soldiers of the Voltan Corps!

916
01:05:22,628 --> 01:05:24,004
Our time has come!

917
01:05:24,547 --> 01:05:27,716
Those racers will be approaching
from three directions.

918
01:05:27,716 --> 01:05:30,886
Split into three groups to counter them!

919
01:05:32,847 --> 01:05:34,849
Volton Corps, move out!

920
01:05:34,849 --> 01:05:35,766
Yes, sir!

921
01:06:41,999 --> 01:06:44,335
I'm going down! Bye-bye!

922
01:06:50,966 --> 01:06:53,302
Here comes God Wing followed by Busties!

923
01:06:53,552 --> 01:06:55,888
Speed Master and Semimaru are right behind.

924
01:06:56,347 --> 01:06:57,556
Here goes!

925
01:06:59,433 --> 01:07:02,811
God Wing makes a splash landing,
immediately going for a counterattack!

926
01:07:04,021 --> 01:07:06,899
What do you do now, Super Boins?

927
01:07:06,899 --> 01:07:08,400
They're blazing away!

928
01:07:08,400 --> 01:07:11,654
You can't counterattack unless
you make a swift landing, first!

929
01:07:12,655 --> 01:07:15,241
Lynchman's gunning for Sonoshee.
Will he catch up?

930
01:07:15,699 --> 01:07:18,536
Johnny! Shoot a Sidewinder
into Crab Sonoshee.

931
01:07:18,702 --> 01:07:19,328
Okay!

932
01:07:34,718 --> 01:07:37,805
Jesus, I'm burning!
That bastard!!

933
01:07:42,476 --> 01:07:43,352
What the hell?!!

934
01:07:47,773 --> 01:07:48,607
Huh?

935
01:07:56,031 --> 01:07:57,116
Fools!

936
01:08:09,461 --> 01:08:10,754
Ow, hoooottt!!

937
01:08:13,424 --> 01:08:14,633
YEEEE-HAAAA!

938
01:08:17,469 --> 01:08:18,262
No way!

939
01:08:20,139 --> 01:08:21,890
Oh, no!

940
01:08:22,808 --> 01:08:25,894
Not bad, Colonel Volton.

941
01:08:26,645 --> 01:08:28,314
Thank you, sir.

942
01:08:30,316 --> 01:08:31,317
What?

943
01:08:35,696 --> 01:08:37,573
I see.

944
01:08:38,574 --> 01:08:42,870
Sir, I just got word we have another problem.

945
01:08:42,870 --> 01:08:44,371
What now?

946
01:08:44,371 --> 01:08:48,208
Observe, please.
REDLINE's broadcast ratings.

947
01:08:48,208 --> 01:08:53,380
82% of the broadcast satellites
in the M3 Nebula...

948
01:08:53,589 --> 01:08:56,425
are uplinked to that
mothership as a terminal...

949
01:08:56,425 --> 01:09:00,095
and are beaming live coverage of
the REDLINE to the entire galaxy.

950
01:09:00,512 --> 01:09:01,972
In other words,

951
01:09:01,972 --> 01:09:05,017
every secret military asset
and facility on Roboworld...

952
01:09:05,017 --> 01:09:08,562
Smash those racers
before they reach...

953
01:09:08,562 --> 01:09:12,066
zone 7X where
Funky Boy is sleeping.

954
01:09:12,983 --> 01:09:14,735
Funky Boy must not be awakened.

955
01:09:14,735 --> 01:09:16,945
He's still a baby
barely out of the womb.

956
01:09:16,945 --> 01:09:20,532
He needs more time
to learn to obey.

957
01:09:26,747 --> 01:09:27,915
Payback time!

958
01:09:38,926 --> 01:09:39,885
Suckers!

959
01:09:51,939 --> 01:09:53,649
Good job, engine three!

960
01:09:54,817 --> 01:09:56,068
Get a load of this!

961
01:09:56,068 --> 01:09:59,697
Crab Sonoshee's bravely
charging up the slope!

962
01:09:59,697 --> 01:10:00,614
Bold move!

963
01:10:00,614 --> 01:10:03,409
She may be able
to take the short cut,

964
01:10:03,409 --> 01:10:06,412
but Lynchcar and the Trans-Am
have to go around.

965
01:10:07,037 --> 01:10:08,539
Johnny! I see the dam!

966
01:10:08,539 --> 01:10:09,957
Here we go!

967
01:10:23,303 --> 01:10:24,680
I see you, Lynchman!

968
01:10:26,473 --> 01:10:30,644
Finally caught up, Cherry Boy Hunter?
I thought you'd retired.

969
01:10:32,187 --> 01:10:33,147
You wish!

970
01:10:33,522 --> 01:10:34,523
Don't celebrate yet!

971
01:10:47,911 --> 01:10:49,538
Yes! Now we're even!

972
01:10:49,830 --> 01:10:52,541
You're making this interesting,
Sonoshee McLaren!

973
01:10:55,335 --> 01:10:56,420
Trava...

974
01:11:02,468 --> 01:11:05,137
Regret leaving me behind in the army?

975
01:11:06,013 --> 01:11:06,805
Captain Deyzuna!

976
01:11:06,805 --> 01:11:07,556
What?

977
01:11:07,556 --> 01:11:09,433
We've spotted a moving target
5 klicks to the west.

978
01:11:09,433 --> 01:11:12,478
Looks like a RED-RACER.

979
01:11:12,478 --> 01:11:15,105
Okay, all vehicles,
move onto the target!

980
01:11:15,314 --> 01:11:16,607
Rogen

981
01:11:16,607 --> 01:11:19,318
This one's mine.
I'm gonna rip his head off!

982
01:11:21,111 --> 01:11:24,990
That weasel!
He thinks he can beat me?

983
01:11:24,990 --> 01:11:29,828
I've been waiting for this
a long time, Trava!

984
01:11:29,828 --> 01:11:32,581
What do you want, Deyzuna?

985
01:11:32,581 --> 01:11:35,167
My sand-biker's gonna
whip your sorry ass!

986
01:11:35,167 --> 01:11:37,628
In your dreams,
you pathetic little shit!

987
01:11:38,754 --> 01:11:40,005
Come and get me!

988
01:11:42,966 --> 01:11:45,302
Now let's check out what JP's up to.

989
01:11:45,302 --> 01:11:48,639
He's finally approaching the dam
way behind the others.

990
01:11:48,639 --> 01:11:51,350
I think it's time for JP to retire.

991
01:11:51,350 --> 01:11:52,142
Yeah, really.

992
01:11:52,142 --> 01:11:56,396
The engine and the machine's
out of balance! Friggin' Frisbee...

993
01:11:57,105 --> 01:11:59,441
What's wrong, JP?

994
01:11:59,441 --> 01:12:01,819
Get her up to speed and you're in the clear.

995
01:12:01,819 --> 01:12:03,487
Don't be afraid to use the gold nitro.

996
01:12:03,487 --> 01:12:05,989
Never thought I'd need this so soon.

997
01:12:11,370 --> 01:12:14,164
Whoa, boy! GO!

998
01:12:20,921 --> 01:12:23,173
He's skipping across!
Do you see that?

999
01:12:23,173 --> 01:12:24,216
I don't believe it!

1000
01:12:24,216 --> 01:12:25,384
Skipping! Do you see this?!

1001
01:12:25,384 --> 01:12:28,887
You gotta hand it to him.
JP's Trans-Am is impressive.

1002
01:12:28,887 --> 01:12:30,722
He's still way behind the rest, though.

1003
01:12:33,016 --> 01:12:36,562
You're late, Frisbee.

1004
01:12:38,021 --> 01:12:40,816
How's your friend doing so far?

1005
01:12:41,567 --> 01:12:43,861
JP's holding the last place as we planned,

1006
01:12:43,861 --> 01:12:46,572
so his odds will stay low.

1007
01:12:46,572 --> 01:12:49,575
He'll make his move in the last quarter,

1008
01:12:49,575 --> 01:12:51,410
get his odds up, then he loses.

1009
01:12:51,410 --> 01:12:54,288
Same as in the YELLOWLINE.
No problem.

1010
01:12:54,288 --> 01:12:59,585
I'm still worried that
he may wanna win the race.

1011
01:12:59,585 --> 01:13:02,421
That will cost me a great deal, you know.

1012
01:13:02,421 --> 01:13:04,548
There's no guarantee, is there?

1013
01:13:04,548 --> 01:13:06,049
You can relax.

1014
01:13:06,049 --> 01:13:09,553
There won't be any surprises.
I guarantee that.

1015
01:13:09,553 --> 01:13:10,637
Noooooo!

1016
01:13:11,388 --> 01:13:13,432
Stop picking on us!

1017
01:13:18,520 --> 01:13:20,188
Oh, no!

1018
01:13:24,359 --> 01:13:25,819
I've had it!

1019
01:13:25,819 --> 01:13:27,279
Let's roll!

1020
01:13:39,207 --> 01:13:40,375
Hi!

1021
01:13:53,180 --> 01:13:54,556
Coochy-coochy-coo.

1022
01:13:58,352 --> 01:14:00,562
What's going on, Big Deyzuna?!

1023
01:14:00,562 --> 01:14:03,273
Two planes were down before I knew it.

1024
01:14:03,273 --> 01:14:05,859
So you lost a couple of planes.
No big deal!

1025
01:14:05,859 --> 01:14:07,611
Use your head!

1026
01:14:07,611 --> 01:14:08,403
Si"

1027
01:14:08,403 --> 01:14:14,826
Dr. Sabose! Quit playing around
with those pervs and tits!

1028
01:14:14,826 --> 01:14:17,329
Wipe out the racers in
the southern sector already!

1029
01:14:17,329 --> 01:14:18,246
Si"

1030
01:14:18,246 --> 01:14:23,043
Little Deyzuna! Who said you could
leave the unit to be in the REDLINE?

1031
01:14:23,043 --> 01:14:24,878
Sorry, sir! I'll do my best.

1032
01:14:25,587 --> 01:14:29,216
Get back in formation
and corner them to Zone 7X!

1033
01:14:30,384 --> 01:14:32,260
Are you reading me,
Little Deyzuna?

1034
01:14:32,511 --> 01:14:35,180
Colonel Volton, please!

1035
01:14:35,180 --> 01:14:36,306
Don't...

1036
01:14:36,306 --> 01:14:38,725
Don't let this punk make a fool of me.

1037
01:14:40,143 --> 01:14:43,855
Stop raving and get a hold of yourself!

1038
01:14:43,855 --> 01:14:45,899
I repeat once more.

1039
01:14:45,899 --> 01:14:49,069
Get back in formation
and chase them to Zone 7X!

1040
01:14:49,069 --> 01:14:50,779
That's an order from your commander!

1041
01:14:51,029 --> 01:14:53,615
I'm afraid I can't take that order, sir.

1042
01:14:53,615 --> 01:14:55,325
I'm entering the race.

1043
01:14:55,325 --> 01:14:57,285
Have you lost your mind?

1044
01:14:57,285 --> 01:15:00,706
You'll be court-martialed and shot!

1045
01:15:00,706 --> 01:15:05,168
Colonel Voltan...
I know the risk, but I must do this.

1046
01:15:05,168 --> 01:15:06,920
I promise victory!

1047
01:15:06,920 --> 01:15:10,173
No! I can't allow that! Deyz...

1048
01:15:10,173 --> 01:15:13,051
Colonel Volton! Are you going
to just stand by and watch?

1049
01:15:13,510 --> 01:15:15,762
Certainly not, Mr. President!

1050
01:15:17,097 --> 01:15:19,182
Attention, all soldiers of Roboworld!

1051
01:15:19,182 --> 01:15:20,767
All units, scramble!

1052
01:15:20,767 --> 01:15:23,770
Intercept all the RED-RACERs in Zone 7X!

1053
01:15:24,771 --> 01:15:27,858
You said all units, Colonel Voltan?

1054
01:15:27,858 --> 01:15:31,486
You heard me!
Send out all units!

1055
01:15:33,530 --> 01:15:37,409
All racers are converging at
the minefield in Zone 7X.

1056
01:15:37,409 --> 01:15:39,578
God Wing takes the lead
in the northern sector,

1057
01:15:39,578 --> 01:15:40,787
followed by Super Boins.

1058
01:15:40,787 --> 01:15:43,081
From southern sector
comes Crab Sonoshee!

1059
01:15:43,081 --> 01:15:45,876
Trava's Speed Master is
coming from the central sector,

1060
01:15:45,876 --> 01:15:48,837
with Little Deyzuna hot on his tail.

1061
01:15:55,552 --> 01:15:59,097
Speed Master's faster than
the detonators on those mines!

1062
01:15:59,097 --> 01:16:00,807
We just got some new footage.

1063
01:16:00,807 --> 01:16:02,934
Gori Rider's burrowing underground.

1064
01:16:02,934 --> 01:16:06,563
The Miki/Todoroki team
is running right behind him.

1065
01:16:06,563 --> 01:16:10,817
It may be a shortcut,
but speed-wise? I'm not sure.

1066
01:16:10,817 --> 01:16:14,488
Ouch! You think we've cleared 7X by now?

1067
01:16:14,863 --> 01:16:18,241
Probably. Let's get out of here
and take them down!

1068
01:16:18,241 --> 01:16:18,825
All right!

1069
01:16:24,206 --> 01:16:25,499
Let's do it, Miki!

1070
01:16:25,791 --> 01:16:27,209
Go get them, Todoroki!

1071
01:16:27,459 --> 01:16:29,377
GUTS AND GLORY!

1072
01:16:30,003 --> 01:16:30,295
You sure about waking it up?

1073
01:16:30,295 --> 01:16:32,839
XXXXXXXpoint (BASE 7x) - UNDERGROUND
You sure about waking it up?

1074
01:16:32,839 --> 01:16:34,382
XXXXXXXpoint (BASE 7X) - UNDERGROUND

1075
01:16:34,382 --> 01:16:37,427
Yeah. The bioweapon asleep
in Roboworld's untouchable area,

1076
01:16:37,427 --> 01:16:38,845
a.k.a. "Funky Boy."

1077
01:16:38,845 --> 01:16:42,724
We have to count on him
to fight Volton's troops.

1078
01:16:43,475 --> 01:16:48,688
Guts and glory! Guts and glory!

1079
01:16:51,066 --> 01:16:52,234
We're coming out!

1080
01:16:54,111 --> 01:16:55,487
Guts and glory!

1081
01:16:55,487 --> 01:16:58,615
There! Miki and Todoroki are making their move!

1082
01:16:58,615 --> 01:17:00,617
They've taken the lead!

1083
01:17:00,867 --> 01:17:03,411
Yes, Miki! We're in the lead!

1084
01:17:04,079 --> 01:17:04,746
Mine!

1085
01:17:10,752 --> 01:17:15,090
Looks like JP's made it to Zone 7X somehow.

1086
01:17:15,090 --> 01:17:17,592
What do you mean "somehow"?

1087
01:17:21,888 --> 01:17:23,348
Frisbee.

1088
01:17:24,307 --> 01:17:26,643
You do know this is business?

1089
01:17:27,435 --> 01:17:29,354
Of course I do.

1090
01:17:36,444 --> 01:17:37,195
Huh?!

1091
01:17:41,491 --> 01:17:43,869
Look, flying carriers!

1092
01:17:43,869 --> 01:17:46,454
I see they've decided to
send in Air-Destroyers.

1093
01:17:46,454 --> 01:17:47,205
Uh-oh!

1094
01:17:47,956 --> 01:17:49,875
Colonel Volton's getting serious.

1095
01:18:07,726 --> 01:18:09,144
He kicked me!

1096
01:18:13,940 --> 01:18:15,150
There's no end to them!

1097
01:18:15,150 --> 01:18:17,444
Ouch, ouch!

1098
01:18:17,444 --> 01:18:18,653
Lynchman!

1099
01:18:18,653 --> 01:18:20,447
Johnny, come closer!

1100
01:18:20,447 --> 01:18:21,239
Okay!

1101
01:18:22,908 --> 01:18:24,826
Todoroki!
Time to use the thunderbolt!

1102
01:18:24,826 --> 01:18:26,036
Rotate 120 degrees!

1103
01:18:26,286 --> 01:18:27,537
Guts and glory!

1104
01:18:32,751 --> 01:18:33,752
Shit, I missed!

1105
01:18:35,629 --> 01:18:37,255
We did it!

1106
01:18:40,717 --> 01:18:41,593
Launch flares!

1107
01:18:50,018 --> 01:18:52,270
That should teach them a lesson.

1108
01:18:52,270 --> 01:18:55,273
Those racers are as good as dead.

1109
01:18:55,273 --> 01:18:57,859
There's no need for any further attack.

1110
01:18:58,568 --> 01:19:01,988
Mr. President.
Did you think I'd stop now?

1111
01:19:01,988 --> 01:19:04,866
You can't afford to
take pity on that scum.

1112
01:19:05,951 --> 01:19:07,118
All right, then.

1113
01:19:30,350 --> 01:19:32,143
Damn, I can't break it!

1114
01:19:32,143 --> 01:19:34,104
Yes, you can!
Smash it with your rage!

1115
01:19:37,482 --> 01:19:40,235
What is this place?!

1116
01:20:06,261 --> 01:20:08,805
I'm coming to get you, Sonoshee.

1117
01:20:22,986 --> 01:20:26,114
What the...?!
That's a bioweapon!

1118
01:20:26,114 --> 01:20:28,908
Isn't that against the
peace treaty, Mr. Minerva?

1119
01:20:28,908 --> 01:20:32,329
I have a feeling we're not
supposed to be seeing this.

1120
01:20:49,512 --> 01:20:50,805
How can Funky Boy be...?!

1121
01:20:50,805 --> 01:20:52,182
I don't believe this!

1122
01:20:52,182 --> 01:20:57,187
Mr. President, Funky Boy
will destroy Roboworld.

1123
01:20:57,437 --> 01:21:00,732
Besides that, that giant bioweapon
is a clear violation of...

1124
01:21:00,732 --> 01:21:04,694
the M3 Nebula Peace Treaty,
and there are no scapegoats to pin this on!

1125
01:21:04,694 --> 01:21:07,614
We must take measures immediately!

1126
01:21:07,614 --> 01:21:09,991
You must make a decision, sir!

1127
01:21:11,409 --> 01:21:12,660
Mr. President!

1128
01:21:13,787 --> 01:21:17,624
Mr. President, we have the
hyper-disintegrator cannons back on line.

1129
01:21:17,624 --> 01:21:20,502
They'll be ready to fire
as soon as charging completes.

1130
01:21:25,590 --> 01:21:28,468
Agghhh...Hail the President!

1131
01:21:29,928 --> 01:21:32,514
Target Funky Boy!
He's out of control!

1132
01:21:32,889 --> 01:21:33,890
Yes, sir.

1133
01:21:39,521 --> 01:21:43,900
Target's set.
We can fire at any time.

1134
01:21:44,567 --> 01:21:47,821
All right.
Take him down in one shot!

1135
01:21:47,821 --> 01:21:49,823
Yes, sir.
Give me the command.

1136
01:21:55,578 --> 01:21:57,622
Fire the hyper-disintegrator cannons!

1137
01:21:57,622 --> 01:21:58,248
Firing!

1138
01:22:25,859 --> 01:22:27,485
Princess!

1139
01:22:30,196 --> 01:22:32,866
Excellent!
We wiped them out clean.

1140
01:22:33,199 --> 01:22:35,535
Energy discharge, complete.

1141
01:22:35,702 --> 01:22:37,120
Now recharging.

1142
01:22:38,455 --> 01:22:40,582
This can't be happening.

1143
01:22:40,582 --> 01:22:41,624
Are they really dead?

1144
01:22:42,292 --> 01:22:43,418
I don't believe this.

1145
01:22:43,793 --> 01:22:46,212
They actually used
hyper-disintegrator cannons.

1146
01:22:47,213 --> 01:22:48,923
It looks like everyone's
been wiped out.

1147
01:22:50,925 --> 01:22:52,969
That bastard planted something!

1148
01:23:00,477 --> 01:23:02,979
Sonoshee, you alright?

1149
01:23:02,979 --> 01:23:03,897
JP.

1150
01:23:05,273 --> 01:23:07,525
You okay, Captain Sabose?

1151
01:23:07,525 --> 01:23:08,693
I'm okay.

1152
01:23:08,693 --> 01:23:10,945
How many planes are left?

1153
01:23:10,945 --> 01:23:13,031
18, including the ones that got damaged.

1154
01:23:13,031 --> 01:23:15,158
16 sand-bikers left in another unit.

1155
01:23:15,158 --> 01:23:17,702
The crossjet unit's been wiped out

1156
01:23:17,702 --> 01:23:21,539
I see... The RED-RACERS
are in equally bad shape.

1157
01:23:21,539 --> 01:23:23,374
Wait for Colonel Volton's orders.

1158
01:23:23,374 --> 01:23:24,167
Roger.

1159
01:23:47,899 --> 01:23:53,112
C'mon, Sonoshee. Winning the
REDLINE's your dream, right?

1160
01:23:54,405 --> 01:23:56,491
I'm only halfway there.

1161
01:23:57,784 --> 01:24:00,370
I didn't get to see the finish line.

1162
01:24:00,370 --> 01:24:05,208
I'll show you. Not much room,
but you don't mind, do you?

1163
01:24:05,208 --> 01:24:08,795
The machine's gonna be too heavy.
You can't win.

1164
01:24:09,504 --> 01:24:10,838
Yes, I will.

1165
01:24:11,172 --> 01:24:14,551
We'll win this together!

1166
01:24:22,559 --> 01:24:27,313
That's sweet, JP,
but I have to ask you something.

1167
01:24:28,773 --> 01:24:32,110
Kinda busy right now!

1168
01:24:32,360 --> 01:24:35,238
No. I need to ask you now.

1169
01:24:37,115 --> 01:24:37,991
Fine!

1170
01:24:38,157 --> 01:24:42,996
Have you been arrested
for fixing a race?

1171
01:24:49,586 --> 01:24:50,587
Yeah.

1172
01:24:50,587 --> 01:24:51,588
What happened?

1173
01:24:54,591 --> 01:24:57,343
It was a Yellow MAX series 8 years ago.

1174
01:24:58,094 --> 01:25:01,222
Our team was on a hot winning streak.

1175
01:25:02,056 --> 01:25:06,102
Frisbee decided to hook up
with the mafia,

1176
01:25:06,102 --> 01:25:09,230
so he could get a
better engine and parts.

1177
01:25:10,690 --> 01:25:15,028
I entered the race
with his life on the line...

1178
01:25:15,028 --> 01:25:16,529
...and I lost.

1179
01:25:16,529 --> 01:25:20,283
After that, he desperately needed the money.

1180
01:25:21,326 --> 01:25:23,870
But there's a sting operation
against the lnuki gang.

1181
01:25:23,870 --> 01:25:27,332
They found stuff pointing to Frisbee.
He was trapped.

1182
01:25:27,332 --> 01:25:30,376
That friggin' Frisbee's gonna get JP killed!

1183
01:25:30,376 --> 01:25:33,588
So you went to prison for him.

1184
01:25:33,588 --> 01:25:37,925
He believed in me and
risked his life so I could race.

1185
01:25:37,925 --> 01:25:40,762
I always owe him for that.

1186
01:25:42,930 --> 01:25:47,060
Then we'll just have to pay him back
by winning the REDLINE.

1187
01:25:51,189 --> 01:25:52,690
You're gonna help me?

1188
01:25:56,110 --> 01:25:59,530
If you help me make
my dream come true.

1189
01:26:00,198 --> 01:26:01,115
Of course.

1190
01:26:16,964 --> 01:26:19,175
This is his regeneration function.

1191
01:26:19,175 --> 01:26:21,678
There must have been
some pieces of him left.

1192
01:26:21,678 --> 01:26:22,804
Secretary Titan!

1193
01:26:22,804 --> 01:26:26,557
Finish him off with the hyper-disintegrator cannons!

1194
01:26:26,557 --> 01:26:30,103
Negative. We need another
two hours to recharge it.

1195
01:26:31,562 --> 01:26:33,690
Where's Volton now?

1196
01:26:33,690 --> 01:26:38,319
I never thought I'd see this day.
Is it ready?

1197
01:26:38,319 --> 01:26:39,404
Yes, it's ready!

1198
01:26:39,404 --> 01:26:41,072
Can we control it?

1199
01:26:41,072 --> 01:26:45,243
With your skill, no problem.

1200
01:26:45,243 --> 01:26:48,913
You just like the idea of
getting new data, don't you?

1201
01:26:48,913 --> 01:26:50,873
Very well. Proceed.

1202
01:26:58,423 --> 01:27:01,551
Oh, no...Princeeeess!

1203
01:27:11,352 --> 01:27:15,273
This feels great! Wonderful!

1204
01:27:15,273 --> 01:27:17,358
I can feel the power!

1205
01:27:29,871 --> 01:27:31,706
Let's get out of here, Shinkai!

1206
01:27:31,706 --> 01:27:32,123
Okay!
Let's get out of here, Shinkai!

1207
01:27:37,962 --> 01:27:40,548
All right! Gori-police custom rider!

1208
01:27:51,517 --> 01:27:55,396
You morons! The RED-RACERS
are running again.

1209
01:27:55,730 --> 01:27:57,899
Go after them, now!

1210
01:27:57,899 --> 01:27:58,900
Yes, sir!

1211
01:27:58,900 --> 01:28:00,318
We should get going.

1212
01:28:02,653 --> 01:28:04,197
This is the machine
your friend tuned up?

1213
01:28:04,197 --> 01:28:04,989
Yeah.

1214
01:28:05,948 --> 01:28:06,866
You ready?

1215
01:28:06,866 --> 01:28:07,408
Yeah.

1216
01:28:17,668 --> 01:28:20,963
Frisbee! With the beefed up stove you gave me,

1217
01:28:20,963 --> 01:28:22,965
Sonoshee and I will blast to the top!

1218
01:28:41,776 --> 01:28:43,986
Your friend has done well.

1219
01:28:45,196 --> 01:28:46,155
Yes.

1220
01:28:46,155 --> 01:28:47,949
It's time we wrapped this up.

1221
01:28:47,949 --> 01:28:50,993
We're in third.
The odds are looking up.

1222
01:28:51,828 --> 01:28:53,579
That should give us enough.

1223
01:28:53,579 --> 01:28:56,916
No point in getting greedy
and ending up in the hole, Frisbee.

1224
01:28:56,916 --> 01:28:59,293
Time to detonate the bomb.

1225
01:28:59,919 --> 01:29:02,672
Wait till JP grabs the lead, please.

1226
01:29:02,672 --> 01:29:04,674
You promised me!

1227
01:29:05,633 --> 01:29:07,176
Then here's a check!

1228
01:29:07,176 --> 01:29:11,556
Double what you got for
the YELLOWLINE race. Take it!

1229
01:29:13,391 --> 01:29:15,142
We're running out of time.

1230
01:29:15,142 --> 01:29:19,480
I'm paying both you and JP enough money.

1231
01:29:19,480 --> 01:29:23,776
What're you complaining about?
Gimme the detonator!

1232
01:29:23,985 --> 01:29:28,906
I want to see this race to the end.
To see us- No...

1233
01:29:29,115 --> 01:29:31,492
I want to see him win!

1234
01:29:37,665 --> 01:29:39,041
Sorry, Frisbee.

1235
01:29:39,041 --> 01:29:42,336
Nothing personal.
It's just business.

1236
01:29:44,839 --> 01:29:47,550
I don't wanna hurt you.
Just hand me the damn thing.

1237
01:29:49,635 --> 01:29:52,138
Over my dead body!

1238
01:29:53,014 --> 01:29:54,932
Suit yourself. You're dead!

1239
01:30:00,855 --> 01:30:01,856
BYE-bye!

1240
01:30:11,240 --> 01:30:13,034
Pops... Why are you here?

1241
01:30:15,286 --> 01:30:17,496
I'll keep this with me for now.
Got that?!

1242
01:30:19,123 --> 01:30:21,500
I didn't come here
to save you!

1243
01:30:21,500 --> 01:30:25,713
But a team mechanic's
gotta see the race through.

1244
01:30:25,713 --> 01:30:27,798
The driver, the mechanic,
and the junk dealer...

1245
01:30:27,798 --> 01:30:31,469
Those three make a team, right?

1246
01:30:34,055 --> 01:30:37,475
God Wing in the lead
is struggling to take control.

1247
01:30:37,475 --> 01:30:40,269
He sustained quite a bit
of damage this time around.

1248
01:30:40,269 --> 01:30:42,271
Hey! Clear the way!

1249
01:30:45,191 --> 01:30:48,069
Machine Head!
Quit tearing up the road!

1250
01:30:50,988 --> 01:30:53,199
I'm having a ball!

1251
01:30:54,158 --> 01:30:55,368
The outside course is clear!

1252
01:30:55,368 --> 01:30:57,411
We can't get there at this speed.

1253
01:30:57,411 --> 01:30:57,995
There!

1254
01:31:00,581 --> 01:31:02,208
Go for it!

1255
01:31:06,712 --> 01:31:07,296
You're here.

1256
01:31:08,214 --> 01:31:09,799
Finally caught up with you.

1257
01:31:09,799 --> 01:31:14,595
You got the guts to use
the steamlight, Sonoshee?

1258
01:31:14,804 --> 01:31:17,598
Huh? That's the same as yours...

1259
01:31:17,807 --> 01:31:19,642
As a courtesy to
stubborn racers like you,

1260
01:31:19,642 --> 01:31:22,103
I won't beat you just yet!

1261
01:31:22,103 --> 01:31:23,396
Bring it on!

1262
01:31:24,897 --> 01:31:28,609
Behold!
The platinum nitro charge!

1263
01:31:36,826 --> 01:31:40,538
And there it is!
Machine Head's Platinum nitro charge!!

1264
01:31:40,913 --> 01:31:43,416
The only man to master the steamlight.

1265
01:31:43,416 --> 01:31:45,543
Looks like the king's gonna win again!

1266
01:31:50,798 --> 01:31:52,299
Hey, Sonoshee!

1267
01:31:52,299 --> 01:31:54,927
We made a deal.
Make my dream come true!

1268
01:32:00,141 --> 01:32:00,850
Second spot is mine!

1269
01:32:05,396 --> 01:32:07,815
Think you can get me?!

1270
01:32:21,746 --> 01:32:24,081
That fool!
He's using steamlight?!

1271
01:32:24,081 --> 01:32:25,624
No man can handle that!

1272
01:32:25,624 --> 01:32:27,334
You can do it, JP!

1273
01:32:27,334 --> 01:32:28,836
Seriously?

1274
01:32:30,087 --> 01:32:30,838
Search me.

1275
01:32:32,923 --> 01:32:34,967
Ow... Hooott!!

1276
01:32:34,967 --> 01:32:38,220
Trying to be funny, huh?
Let's see what he's got.

1277
01:32:39,430 --> 01:32:41,515
Let's roll, Todoroki!

1278
01:32:41,515 --> 01:32:42,349
Guts and glory!

1279
01:32:45,686 --> 01:32:47,438
Sorry, Deyzuna. Time's up.

1280
01:32:48,355 --> 01:32:49,732
Let's go, Shinkai!

1281
01:32:49,732 --> 01:32:50,858
Here we come!

1282
01:32:51,776 --> 01:32:53,110
Don't leave me!

1283
01:33:07,666 --> 01:33:08,542
No way.

1284
01:33:09,418 --> 01:33:11,295
We'll never catch up with them.

1285
01:33:11,295 --> 01:33:12,421
Hold on a minute, Mr. Minerva!

1286
01:33:12,421 --> 01:33:13,214
Huh?

1287
01:33:13,214 --> 01:33:16,926
The finish line's on top
of the Dest Tower, isn't it?

1288
01:33:16,926 --> 01:33:21,138
No one can climb up the wall to reach the line!

1289
01:33:21,138 --> 01:33:21,722
What'll they do?

1290
01:33:22,389 --> 01:33:23,766
Princess, what's...?

1291
01:33:23,766 --> 01:33:25,226
Watch and see.

1292
01:33:33,734 --> 01:33:35,027
What the...?!

1293
01:33:35,027 --> 01:33:36,237
Check this out!

1294
01:33:36,237 --> 01:33:39,740
The REDLINE mothership has warped out
beneath the Dest Tower...

1295
01:33:39,907 --> 01:33:41,742
and became the final straightway!

1296
01:33:43,035 --> 01:33:44,245
You see it now?

1297
01:33:44,620 --> 01:33:48,749
The final straightway has
been joined to the finish line!

1298
01:33:52,044 --> 01:33:53,963
Ugh... Sonoshee...

1299
01:33:55,005 --> 01:33:56,173
Let's do it!

1300
01:34:04,056 --> 01:34:07,059
JP's moving up like a bullet!
What's going on?

1301
01:34:07,059 --> 01:34:09,812
Unbelievable!
This is unbelievable!

1302
01:34:11,188 --> 01:34:14,275
I'm gonna win.

1303
01:34:14,275 --> 01:34:17,987
I'm the king of kings!
You know what that means, JP?

1304
01:34:17,987 --> 01:34:21,157
It means victory belongs to me!

1305
01:34:21,157 --> 01:34:25,536
I'm gonna win.
I've got a goddess at my side!

1306
01:34:32,501 --> 01:34:36,714
Here they come!
Here come JP and Sonoshee!

1307
01:34:57,401 --> 01:34:58,485
I see it!

1308
01:35:08,454 --> 01:35:13,542
JP! You need an edge
to win the REDLINE!

1309
01:35:13,542 --> 01:35:16,337
You don't deserve to win this race!

1310
01:35:19,006 --> 01:35:23,302
Goddamn it! I need something
to juice this thing up...!

1311
01:35:23,302 --> 01:35:25,846
Frisbee! ls there anything?!

1312
01:35:25,846 --> 01:35:27,681
There's nothing left!

1313
01:35:35,606 --> 01:35:38,901
Whoa! JP's engine has blown!
It's blown!

1314
01:35:39,276 --> 01:35:41,570
But wait...
He's picking up speed somehow.

1315
01:36:11,558 --> 01:36:13,686
Victory's mine, JP!

1316
01:36:17,648 --> 01:36:18,732
JP!

1317
01:36:18,899 --> 01:36:19,775
Sonoshee!

1318
01:36:57,354 --> 01:36:59,815
It's JP and Sonoshee!
They're the winners!

1319
01:37:00,107 --> 01:37:06,113
JP and Sonoshee! JP and Sonoshee
came in top at the finish line!

1320
01:37:06,113 --> 01:37:08,115
JP! JP!

1321
01:37:08,115 --> 01:37:10,034
Sonoshee! Sonoshee!

1322
01:37:10,367 --> 01:37:12,161
He's done it!

1323
01:37:21,378 --> 01:37:23,630
Interesting...

1324
01:37:32,473 --> 01:37:34,516
Oh... That's beautiful.

1325
01:37:38,812 --> 01:37:40,022
Sonoshee.

1326
01:37:41,357 --> 01:37:43,108
I love you.

1327
01:37:43,609 --> 01:37:46,195
I love you, too, JP.
